media: i2c: ov48b2q: add a 2000x1500 mode

A second mode, 2000x1500 (the 4000x3000 output binned again), up to 90
fps and 30 fps by default, for consumers that cannot keep up with 12 MP:
libcamera's software ISP manages 4000x3000 at about 15 fps.

The registers that differ between the vendor's (Qualcomm CamX module data)
4000x3000 and 2000x1500 settings, written after the 4000x3000 table; their
PLL registers (0x0305, 0x0345, 0x4837) are left out, so the clocks stay as
MediaTek's table sets them: the same 900 MHz link and 115.2 MHz timing
clock, 768 clocks a line. Like MediaTek's binned 1280x720 table, the frame
length copies at 0x381a-0x3827 are not written.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

